---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '') + '/';
const site = import.meta.env.SITE.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | OtakuList"
  description="Privacy information for OtakuList, including how we handle local watchlist data and browser storage."
  canonical={`${site}${base}privacy-policy.html`}
  page="privacy"
>
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 py-16 text-[#f4f2f8]">
    <div class="mb-8">
      <p class="mb-3 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-[#a78bfa]">OtakuList</p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-black tracking-[-0.04em] md:text-5xl">Privacy Policy</h1>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-8 rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.04] p-6 md:p-8">
      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-3 text-2xl font-bold tracking-[-0.03em]">Summary</h2>
        <p class="text-[15px] leading-7 text-[#f4f2f8]/70">
          OtakuList is designed to keep your anime watchlist local to your browser. We do not require an account and we
          do not sell your data. Cloud sync is entirely optional: while you are logged out, nothing about your list ever
          leaves your device. If you do create an account, your list is stored in a single private record that only your
          own login can read.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-3 text-2xl font-bold tracking-[-0.03em]">What data we store</h2>
        <p class="text-[15px] leading-7 text-[#f4f2f8]/70">
          The extension stores your watchlist in your browser's local storage. This includes anime titles, episode
          counts, status (Watching, Completed, etc.), and related list information you choose to save.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[15px] leading-7 text-[#f4f2f8]/70">
            Each saved entry also records the address of the page you last watched that anime on, which is what the
            <b>Resume</b> button opens. That address includes the site's domain.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[15px] leading-7 text-[#f4f2f8]/70">
            By default all of this is kept on your device. If you choose to log in — either on the Anime List page or from
            the extension popup — the same entries, <em>including those page addresses</em>, are mirrored to a private
            Supabase record that only your authenticated account can access. If you would prefer that information never
            leave your machine, simply do not log in; every other feature behaves identically. Logging out stops the
            syncing and leaves your list on your device.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[15px] leading-7 text-[#f4f2f8]/70">
            Creating an account also means we hold the email address you signed up with (or the one your Google account
            provides), because that is what identifies the account. The optional Gacha Profiles feature stores whatever
            you put on your profile — and that profile is <b>public by design</b>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-3 text-2xl font-bold tracking-[-0.03em]">What we do not collect</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 text-[15px] leading-7 text-[#f4f2f8]/70">
          <li>We do not require user accounts — the extension and the web list work fully without one.</li>
          <li>We do not track your browsing. The extension inspects a page to detect the anime on it; it never records
            a history of the pages you visit.</li>
          <li>We do not sell, rent, or trade your list information.</li>
          <li>We do not run any analytics, telemetry or advertising on the site or in the extension.</li>
          <li>We do not read your list. Row-level security means a synced list is readable only by the account that
            wrote it.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-3 text-2xl font-bold tracking-[-0.03em]">External data requests</h2>
        <p class="text-[15px] leading-7 text-[#f4f2f8]/70">
          In order to identify titles and fetch anime metadata such as cover art or official name data, the extension may
          access public metadata services such as AniList. These requests are made to provide better title matching and a
          cleaner watchlist experience. This is not used to create a user profile or track personal browsing behavior.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-3 text-2xl font-bold tracking-[-0.03em]">Website usage</h2>
        <p class="text-[15px] leading-7 text-[#f4f2f8]/70">
            The OtakuList website does not require an account for local list management. Account creation is optional and
            is used to provide cloud sync for your anime list and the separate Gacha Profiles feature. We do not use your
            watchlist for advertising or personal browsing tracking.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-3 text-2xl font-bold tracking-[-0.03em]">Your control</h2>
        <p class="text-[15px] leading-7 text-[#f4f2f8]/70">
          You can remove your saved data by clearing your browser's site data or removing the extension. On Chromium
          browsers, you can also delete the extension's stored data from the browser storage settings.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-3 text-2xl font-bold tracking-[-0.03em]">Contact</h2>
        <p class="text-[15px] leading-7 text-[#f4f2f8]/70">
          If you have any privacy questions, email us at <a href="mailto:thandermughal@gmail.com" class="text-[#a78bfa] underline">thandermughal@gmail.com</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
